[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Blackmar-Diemer Gambit"]
[Variation "Blackmar-Diemer Gambit Accepted, Euwe Defense"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "gambit,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "take-the-pawns,develop-first"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Opponent "2.e4"]
[Start "1. d4 d5"]

2. e4 dxe4 { Take it. The pawn is free, and White gets only quick development in return. } 3. Nc3 Nf6 { Develops and defends the extra pawn on e4, so White has to spend a move to attack it again. } 4. f3 { The gambit move: White offers a second pawn for open lines and quick development. } ( 4. Bg5 Bf5 5. f3 Nbd7 6. g4 Bg6 7. Qe2 ) 4... exf3 { Keep the second pawn too. Black can give material back later, but only for a clear reason such as a safe king. } 5. Nxf3 e6 { Solid: it opens the f8 bishop and covers d5 and f5. Black is two pawns up, so the job is to develop, castle and avoid fancy lines. } 6. Bd3 Be7 { Gets ready to castle. The bishop can also go to d6 if White's pieces aim at the kingside. } 7. Qe2 O-O { The king is safe before White can build an attack on it. } 8. Bf4 Nc6 { Attacks d4 and prepares ...Nb4, which hits the bishop on d3 and eyes c2. } 9. O-O-O Nb4 { Hits the bishop on d3 and eyes c2, so the bishop must leave or be traded. } 10. Rhe1 Nxd3+ { Trades off White's best attacking piece, the bishop aimed at h7. } 11. Qxd3 Nd5 { Gets the knight to a strong central square and offers to swap off White's pieces. } 12. Nxd5 exd5 { Plan: keep trading pieces, because the two extra pawns count most in a simpler position. If White attacks the king, give a pawn back with ...c5 to open the centre. } *
